  "id": "Compound::DB01085 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Pilocarpine is linked to Chrm2 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve cholinergic muscarinic receptors. The evidence suggests that Pilocarpine, as a cholinergic muscarinic agonist, binds to Chrm2, with Bethanechol and Carbachol acting as intermediates in this relationship. Both Bethanechol and Carbachol are classified under the broader category of carboxylic esters, which are known to interact with muscarinic receptors. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Chrm2, along with the shared lowest common ancestors in the graph, supports a consistent mechanism of action involving muscarinic receptor activation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of cholinergic signaling in the modulation of Chrm2, with Pilocarpine potentially exerting its effects through similar mechanisms as Bethanechol and Carbachol. The evidence underscores the importance of cholinergic agonists in influencing muscarinic receptor function, particularly in the context of nervous system activity.",
